      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There are few reports on the prevalence of headache in Parkinson's disease (PD). In the present study, 223 chronic PD sufferers and 291 controls are surveyed by a headache questionnaire. There is no significant difference in the total prevalence of headache in sex and age-matched patients and controls. However, male patients with PD have a higher prevalence of moderate to severe migraine than the control population."},
